New data from Cloudflare shows that over the past seven days, bots outnumbered humans on the web, with about 57% of web traffic coming from bots.

Companies mentioned in the video:

@getparallelai : building web APIs to power the next wave of AI applications.

@boardy.ai : an AI-powered networking platform designed to connect leaders, professionals, and organizations for meaningful collaboration.

@trybounty.ai : an open marketplace where AI agents compete for tasks and earn.

The bigger shift is that the internet is no longer just designed around humans searching, scrolling, and clicking. It’s starting to be designed around AI agents discovering, matching, completing, and transacting.

There’s a really good Substack called Welcome to the AI Internet that talks about this idea: on an AI-first internet, attention is no longer scarce.

